module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.AssociatedSiteRefinement
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.FlatFppfInclusion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.Quasicoherent.BaseSites

/-!
# Covering sieves of a flat object are refined by coverings with flat sources

Let `𝒳` be an algebraic stack over a scheme `S` in a big fppf site `B`, let `τ` be one of the
five topologies of **Stacks 06TP**, and let `x` be a *flat* object of `𝒳` in the sense of
**Stacks 0787**. This file proves that every `τ`-covering sieve of `x` contains a `τ`-covering
family all of whose sources are again flat objects.

That statement is what makes a vanishing condition imposed at the flat objects only — the
parasitic condition of **Stacks 0773** — a *local* condition at a flat object, and it is the
geometric input of clause (2) of **Stacks 0774**: the source's "if `{x_i → x}` is a `τ`-covering
and `x` lies over a scheme flat over `𝒳`, then so does each `x_i`, because the `τ`-coverings of
schemes are flat".

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.flatArrows`: the members of a sieve of schemes whose underlying morphism is
  flat.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.generate_flatArrows_mem_toGrothendieck`: for a collection of covering
  families of schemes contained in the fppf one, the flat members of a covering sieve already
  generate a covering sieve.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.generate_flatArrows_mem_baseTopology` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_flatCovering_le_of_mem_baseOverTopology`: the same for
  each of the five topologies of **Stacks 03FF**, and after localization at `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_flatObject_covering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology`: the
  statement upstairs — a `τ`-covering sieve of a flat object of `𝒳` contains a `τ`-covering
  family with flat sources.

## Implementation notes

The content is the first result, and the shape in which it is proved matters. One cannot simply
intersect a covering family with the flat morphisms: the members of a covering *sieve* of
`B.baseTopology τ` need not be flat, since a sieve contains all composites with its members and
the saturation producing the topology from the chosen covering families of **Stacks 03FF** adds
sieves that are only *refined* by such a family. What is true is that the flat part of a
covering sieve — a subcollection, not a sieve — generates a covering sieve, and that is proved by
induction over `CategoryTheory.Precoverage.Saturate`, the inductive presentation of the topology
generated by a collection of covering families. The four cases are: the chosen families, whose
members are flat by **Stacks 021R**; the top sieve, which contains the identity; a pullback,
where the flat part is pulled back along the base change of its members, flatness being stable
under base change; and the local character, where the flat parts compose, flatness being stable
under composition. No stability property of the chosen collection itself is needed, which is
what lets the single induction serve all five topologies: for the Zariski, étale, smooth and
syntomic ones the corresponding stability statements are not available.

Passing from the base to the localization at `S` and then to `𝒳` adds nothing: the first step is
`CategoryTheory.Sieve.overEquiv`, and the second is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_chosenCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology`, which refines a
covering sieve upstairs by a family whose image is a chosen family downstairs for *any* class of
chosen families, here the class "all members flat, and the family generates a covering sieve".
Flatness of the sources upstairs is then `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.flatObject_of_flat`, and that
the family covers upstairs is `CategoryTheory.Functor.inheritedPrecoverage` together with the
fact that in a category fibred in groupoids every morphism is strongly cartesian.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 021R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03FF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03FF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06NU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06NU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06TP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06TP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0773](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0773)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0774](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0774)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0787](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0787)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

universe u w

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u})

/-- The members of a sieve of schemes of a big fppf site whose underlying morphism of schemes is
flat. This is a collection of covering morphisms, not a sieve: it is not stable under
precomposition with a non-flat morphism. -/
def flatArrows {X : B.Schemes} (T : Sieve X) : Presieve X :=
  fun _ f => T f ∧ Flat (B.inclusion.map f)

/-- The base change along an arbitrary morphism of a flat morphism of the big fppf category is
flat: the inclusion into schemes preserves fibre products, and flatness of morphisms of schemes
is stable under base change. -/
@[sga "3 VIB 11.1" "(b), special case"]
private theorem flat_inclusion_map_pullback_snd {W X Y : B.Schemes} (w : W ⟶ X) (f : Y ⟶ X)
    [Flat (B.inclusion.map w)] : Flat (B.inclusion.map (pullback.snd w f)) := by
  have : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan B.inclusion := inferInstance
  rw [← PreservesPullback.iso_hom_snd B.inclusion w f]
  infer_instance

/-- **The flat members of a covering sieve of schemes already generate a covering sieve.**

Here the topology is the one generated by an arbitrary collection of covering families contained
in the fppf collection of the ambient big fppf site, so that each member of such a family is flat
by **Stacks 021R**. No stability property of the collection is assumed; see the implementation
notes for why, and for the four cases of the induction. -/
theorem generate_flatArrows_mem_toGrothendieck {K : Precoverage B.Schemes}
    (hK : K ≤ B.precoverage) {X : B.Schemes} {T : Sieve X}
    (hT : T ∈ K.toGrothendieck X) :
    Sieve.generate (flatArrows B T) ∈ K.toGrothendieck X := by
  rw [Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff] at hT
  induction hT with
  | of Y R hR =>
      refine K.toGrothendieck.superset_covering ?_
        (Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck hR)
      rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff]
      intro Z g hg
      exact ⟨Z, 𝟙 Z, g, ⟨⟨Z, 𝟙 Z, g, hg, by simp⟩,
        (Stack.flat_and_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_mem_precoverage B R (hK _ hR) g hg).1⟩,
        by simp⟩
  | top Y =>
      refine K.toGrothendieck.superset_covering ?_ (K.toGrothendieck.top_mem Y)
      intro Z k _
      refine ⟨Y, k, 𝟙 Y, ⟨trivial, ?_⟩, by simp⟩
      rw [B.inclusion.map_id]
      infer_instance
  | pullback Y T hT Z f ih =>
      refine K.toGrothendieck.superset_covering ?_
        (K.toGrothendieck.pullback_stable f ih)
      intro V g hg
      obtain ⟨W, h, w, ⟨hwT, hwflat⟩, hcomp⟩ := hg
      have : Flat (B.inclusion.map w) := hwflat
      refine ⟨pullback w f, pullback.lift h g hcomp, pullback.snd w f,
        ⟨?_, flat_inclusion_map_pullback_snd B w f⟩, pullback.lift_snd _ _ _⟩
      rw [Sieve.pullback_apply, ← pullback.condition]
      exact T.downward_closed hwT _
  | transitive Y T R hT hR ihT ihR =>
      refine K.toGrothendieck.transitive ihT _ ?_
      rintro V g ⟨W, h, w, ⟨hwT, hwflat⟩, rfl⟩
      refine K.toGrothendieck.superset_covering ?_
        (K.toGrothendieck.pullback_stable h (ihR hwT))
      rintro U k ⟨P, m, v, ⟨hvR, hvflat⟩, hcomp⟩
      have : Flat (B.inclusion.map w) := hwflat
      have : Flat (B.inclusion.map v) := hvflat
      refine ⟨P, m, v ≫ w, ⟨hvR, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
      · rw [B.inclusion.map_comp]
        infer_instance
      · rw [← Category.assoc, hcomp, Category.assoc]

namespace BigFppfSite

/-- **The flat members of a covering sieve of one of the five big sites of Stacks 03FF already
generate a covering sieve.** Each of the five topologies is generated by a collection of covering
families contained in the fppf one, so this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.generate_flatArrows_mem_toGrothendieck` read five times. -/
theorem generate_flatArrows_mem_baseTopology (τ : SiteKind) {X : B.Schemes} {T : Sieve X}
    (hT : T ∈ B.baseTopology τ X) :
    Sieve.generate (flatArrows B T) ∈ B.baseTopology τ X := by
  cases τ
  case fppf => exact generate_flatArrows_mem_toGrothendieck B le_rfl hT
  all_goals
    exact generate_flatArrows_mem_toGrothendieck B
      (B.chosenPrecoverage_le_precoverage fun _ hE => hE.1) hT

end BigFppfSite

namespace BigFppfOver

variable (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **A covering sieve of one of the five localized big sites over `S` contains a covering family
of flat morphisms.** The family is produced as a pre-`0`-hypercover indexed by the flat members of
the sieve itself, and the class it is asserted to belong to — all members flat, and the generated
sieve covering — is the one
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_chosenCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology` is fed with
upstairs. -/
theorem exists_flatCovering_le_of_mem_baseOverTopology (τ : SiteKind)
    {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {R : Sieve U}
    (hR : R ∈ BigFppfOver.baseOverTopology B S hS τ U) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} U,
      ((∀ i, Flat (B.inclusion.map (E.f i).left)) ∧
          Sieve.generate E.presieve₀ ∈ BigFppfOver.baseOverTopology B S hS τ U) ∧
        E.presieve₀ ≤ R.arrows := by
  -- the flat part of `R`, upstairs
  let W : Presieve U := fun _ f => R f ∧ Flat (B.inclusion.map f.left)
  let E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} U := ⟨W.uncurry, fun i => i.1.1, fun i => i.1.2⟩
  have hE : E.presieve₀ = W := by
    funext V g
    exact propext ⟨fun ⟨i⟩ => i.2, fun hg => .mk (⟨⟨V, g⟩, hg⟩ : W.uncurry)⟩
  refine ⟨E, ⟨fun i => i.2.2, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · -- the generated sieve covers, by the statement downstairs
    rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff] at hR ⊢
    refine (B.baseTopology τ).superset_covering ?_
      (BigFppfSite.generate_flatArrows_mem_baseTopology B τ hR)
    rintro V g ⟨Z, h, w, ⟨hwR, hwflat⟩, rfl⟩
    rw [Sieve.overEquiv_iff] at hwR ⊢
    refine ⟨Over.mk (w ≫ U.hom), Over.homMk h (by simp), Over.homMk w rfl, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [hE]
      exact ⟨hwR, hwflat⟩
    · ext
      simp
  · rw [hE]
    exact fun _ _ hg => hg.1

end BigFppfOver

namespace Stack

variable (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S) (𝒳 : Stack.AlgebraicStacks.{u, w} B S hS)
  (τ : SiteKind)

/-- **Every `τ`-covering sieve of a flat object of an algebraic stack contains a `τ`-covering
family whose sources are flat objects.**

This is the geometric input of clause (2) of **Stacks 0774**. The family is obtained from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_chosenCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology` at the class of
covering families of `(Sch/S)_τ` consisting of flat morphisms, which
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_flatCovering_le_of_mem_baseOverTopology` supplies; its
sources are flat objects by `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.flatObject_of_flat`, and it is a covering
family of the site of **Stacks 06TP** because its image covers and because every morphism of a
category fibred in groupoids is strongly cartesian. -/
theorem exists_flatObject_covering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology
    {x : 𝒳.val.val.obj} (hx : flatObject B S hS 𝒳.val x) (T : Sieve x)
    (hT : T ∈ BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p τ x) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} x,
      (∀ i, flatObject B S hS 𝒳.val (E.X i)) ∧
        Sieve.generate E.presieve₀ ∈
          BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p τ x ∧
        E.presieve₀ ≤ T.arrows := by
  obtain ⟨E, ⟨hflat, hcov⟩, hle⟩ := exists_chosenCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology
    B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p (B.baseTopology τ)
    (fun F => (∀ i, Flat (B.inclusion.map (F.2.f i).left)) ∧
      Sieve.generate F.2.presieve₀ ∈ BigFppfOver.baseOverTopology B S hS τ F.1)
    (fun _ _ hR =>
      BigFppfOver.exists_flatCovering_le_of_mem_baseOverTopology B S hS τ hR)
    𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids T hT
  refine ⟨E, fun i => flatObject_of_flat B S hS 𝒳 (E.f i) (hflat i) hx, ?_, hle⟩
  apply Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck
  refine ⟨fun _ f _ => 𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids.isStronglyCartesian f, ?_⟩
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff]
  simpa only [PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map] using hcov

end Stack

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
